STEPS IN MACHINE LEARNING MODEL DEVELOPMENT
==============================================

1. PROBLEM DEFINITION
Define what you want to solve. Identify input & output, set objectives.

2. DATA COLLECTION
Gather relevant data from various sources (databases, APIs, sensors, etc.).

3. EXPLORATORY DATA ANALYSIS (EDA)
Analyze data to understand patterns, distributions, correlations, missing values.

4. DATA PREPROCESSING / CLEANING
Handle missing values, remove outliers, fix errors, standardize formats.

5. FEATURE SELECTION & ENGINEERING
Select important features, create new features, remove redundant ones.

6. SPLIT THE DATASET
Divide data into training (70%), validation (15%), testing (15%) sets.

7. MODEL SELECTION
Choose appropriate algorithm (Regression, Classification, Clustering, etc.).

8. MODEL TRAINING
Train the selected model on training data to learn patterns.

9. MODEL EVALUATION
Evaluate model performance on validation data using metrics (accuracy, precision, etc.).

10. HYPERPARAMETER TUNING
Adjust model parameters to improve performance.

11. MODEL TESTING / VALIDATION
Test final model on test data to check real-world performance.

---

SUMMARY:
Define → Collect → Analyze → Clean → Engineer → Split → Select → Train → Evaluate → Tune → Test
